From d1774517939de49e175280ed49c97843f63d89eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:34:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Worker (employee) accounts: add days, routes and
 documents on assigned projects

- Workers get the site-capture workspace at Upload for the projects their
  company assigns them: upload footage for a day, draw and delete flight
  routes for a date, link route videos, edit footage details, and a new
  Documents tab to upload and edit project documents.
- Server checks: paths, route videos, document upload/edit and flight edit
  now accept active company members, each guarded by require_project_editor
  (company admins: any company project; workers: assigned projects only).
  Admin-only tools are unchanged: client access codes, team, billing,
  project setup/boundary/site image, and deleting flights or documents.
  Admin-only controls are hidden in the worker workspace.
- Fix: the employee tenant scope filtered every tenant model by project,
  which crashed on models without one (StorageReservation), so worker
  uploads through local storage silently saved nothing. Models without a
  project are now scoped by company only.
- After saving, workers return to their workspace instead of the admin page.
- Tests: tests/test_worker_accounts.py (7).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HbptFaAKPeT417LTNgj5bU
